===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|en|uttermost}}

===Etymology===
{{PIE word|en|úd}}{{root|en|ine-pro|*meh₂-|id=good}}
From {{inh|en|enm|utmost}}, {{m|enm|utemest}}{{nb...|otemeste, otemost, ottemeste, ottemoste, vttemest, vtmest, (Northern England) vtmast, (Scotland) vtmast, vtmest|otherforms=1}}, from {{inh|en|ang|ūtmest}}, {{m|ang|ūtemest}}{{nb...|(Northumbria) wutmest|otherforms=1}}, from {{m|ang|ūt}}, {{m|ang|ūte|t=out; outdoors, outside}} + {{m|ang|-mest|pos={{glossary|suffix}} meaning ‘furthest’, used to form {{glossary|superlative}}s of some {{glossary|adjective}}s}} (and conflated with {{m|en|most}}). {{m|ang||Ūt}} is derived from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*ūt|t=out, outward}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*úd|t=out, outward}}.<ref>{{R:OED Online|pos=adj.'' and ''n|id=220782|date=1926|nodot=1}}; {{R:Lexico|pos=adj.'' and ''n}}</ref> Equivalent to {{suffix|en|out|most}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈʌtməʊ̯st/|/ˈʌtməst/|a=RP}}
* {{enPR|ŭt'mōst|a=GA}}, {{IPA|en|/ˈʌtmoʊ̯st/|[ˈʌʔ-]|[ˈət-]}}
* {{audio|en|En-us-utmost.ogg|a=GA}}
* {{hyphenation|en|ut|most}}

===Adjective===
{{head|en|superlative adjective}}

# {{en-superlative of|utter}}; [[situate#Verb|situated]] at the [[most]] [[distant]] [[limit#Noun|limit]]; [[farthest]], [[outermost]].
#: {{synonyms|en|outmost|uttermost|yondermost}}
#: {{ux|en|the '''utmost''' limits of the land}}
#: {{ux|en|the '''utmost''' extent of human knowledge}}
#* {{RQ:Herbert Temple|chapter=The Sacrifice|page=26|passage=Betwixt two thieves I &#91;{{w|Jesus}}&#93; ſpend my '''utmoſt''' breath, / As he that for ſome robberie ſuffereth.}}
#* {{RQ:Evelyn Diary|volume=I|entrydate=11 October 1644|page=72|passage=[W]e coaſted within 2 leagues of Antibes, which is the '''utmoſt''' towne in France.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=w:Danby Pickering|chapter=Cap. IX. An Act to Explain and Amend Two Acts of Parliament,{{nb...|One Made in the Twelfth and the Other in the Thirteenth Year of His Late Majesty’s Reign}}, for Making Navigable the River Dun in the County of York,{{nb...|and for the Better Perfecting and Maintaining the Said Navigation, and for Uniting the Said Proprietors thereof into One Company.}}|title=The Statutes at Large, from the Second to the 9th Year of [[w:George II of Great Britain|King George II]].{{nb...|To which is Prefixed, a Table Containing the Titles of All the Statutes during that Period.}}|location=Cambridge, Cambridgeshire|publisher={{...|Printed by}} Joseph Bentham,{{nb...|printer to the University}}; for Charles Bathurst,{{nb...|at the Cross-Keys, opposite St. Dunstan’s Church in Fleet-Street, London.}}|year=1733|year_published=1765|volume=XVI|page=370|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=SlQDAAAAQAAJ&pg=PA370|oclc=1015505952|passage=[T]he maſters, wardens, ſearchers, aſſiſtants and commonalty of the company of cutlers in ''Hallamſhire'' in the county of ''York'', their ſucceſſors and aſſigns, are nominated and appointed undertakers of the ſaid navigation, with power to make the ſaid river navigable, at their own expence, from ''Holmſtile'' aforeſaid, up the ſaid river above ''Holmſtile'' to the '''utmoſt''' extent of ''Tinſley'' westward, [...]}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Professor Larrabee|title=The Heavens|editor=W. C. Larrabee|magazine=[[w:The Ladies' Repository|The Ladies’ Repository: A Monthly Periodical, Devoted to Literature and Religion]]|location=Cincinnati, Oh.|publisher=L. Swormstedt and A. Poe;{{nb...|New York, N.Y.: T. Carlton and Z. Phillips; R. P. Thompson, printer.}}|month=March|year=1852|volume=XII|page=109|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=JBoAAAAAYAAJ&pg=PA109|column=1|oclc=247142692|passage=As yet we are far from having explored the '''utmost''' depths of space. Our telescopes have only reached a limited distance into the regions of the heavens.}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|-}}

# The most [[extreme]]; [[great#Adjective|greatest]], [[ultimate#Adjective|ultimate]].
#: {{syn|en|intense|maximal|uttermost|Thesaurus:extreme}}
#: {{ux|en|the '''utmost''' assiduity}}
#: {{ux|en|the '''utmost''' harmony}}
#: {{ux|en|the '''utmost''' misery or happiness}}
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Coriolanus|act=III|scene=i|page=17|column=1|passage=Ile go to him, and vndertake to bring him in peace, / Where he ſhall anſwer by a lawfull Forme, / (In peace) to his '''vtmoſt''' perill.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Jerome Osorio [''i.e.'', {{w|Jerónimo Osório}}]|chapter=Book XI|translator=w:James Gibbs|title=The History of the Portuguese, during the Reign of Emmanuel:{{nb...|Containing All Their Discoveries, from the Coast of Africk to the Farthest Part of China; Their Battles by Sea and Land, Their Sieges, and Other Memorable Exploits: With a Description of Those Countries, and a Particular Account of the Religion, Government, and Customs of the Natives. Including also, the Discovery of the Brazils, and Their Wars with the Moors. Written Originally in Latin by Jerome Osorio, Bishop of Sylves. Now First Translated into English by James Gibbs.}}|location=London|publisher={{...|Printed for}} [[w:Andrew Millar|A[ndrew] Millar]],{{nb...|in the Strand.}}|year=1752|volume=II|page=239|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=faM2AAAAMAAJ&pg=PA239|oclc=1003956408|passage=She was a lady adorned with many noble virtues: the '''utmoſt''' ſtrictneſs in her life and morals, eaſy and affable in her behaviour, and agreeably modeſt in her converſation.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=[[w:William Bingley|W[illiam] Bingley]]|title=Animal Biography, or, Popular Zoology;{{nb...|Illustrated by Authentic Anecdotes of the Economy, Habits of Life, Instincts, and Sagacity, of the Animal Creation. [...] In Four Volumes.}}|edition=6th|location=London|publisher={{...|Printed for}} [[w:Rivington (publishers)|C[harles] and J[ohn] Rivington]]; [...]|year=1824|volume=II (Mammiferous Animals—Birds)|pages=26–27|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=A_lDAQAAMAAJ&pg=PA27|oclc=82377449|passage=The migrations of the Economic Rats, are not less extraordinary than those of the Lemmings. In the spring of the year they collect together in amazing numbers, and proceed in a course directly westward; swimming with the '''utmost''' intrepidity over rivers, lakes, and even arms of the sea.}}
#* {{RQ:Dickens Martin Chuzzlewit|chapter=Wherein Certain Persons are Presented to the Reader, with Whom He may, if He Please, Become Better Acquainted|page=16|passage="Bah!" cried John Westlock, with the '''utmost''' disgust and disdain the monosyllable is capable of expressing.}}
#* {{RQ:Whitman Leaves of Grass|poem=I Sing the Body Electric|collection=Children of Adam|stanza=6|page=84|passage=The wildest largest passions, bliss that is '''utmost''', sorrow that is '''utmost''' become him well, pride is for him, / The full-spread pride of man is calming and excellent to the soul, [...]}}
#* {{RQ:G&M|author=James Adams|title=Group of who? A new book paints the fullest picture yet of Canada’s vision of Impressionism|date=5 December 2014|url=https://www.theglobeandmail.com/arts/art-and-architecture/group-of-who-a-new-book-paints-the-fullest-picture-yet-of-canadas-vision-of-impressionism/article21967828/
|passage=As these monographs and as these occasional exhibition catalogues on some handful of Canadian Impressionists started to appear, once again, I was surprised (to say it with the '''utmost''' respect) that they were aberrated, there was no timeline, there was no continuity.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20150110100740/https://www.theglobeandmail.com/arts/art-and-architecture/group-of-who-a-new-book-paints-the-fullest-picture-yet-of-canadas-vision-of-impressionism/article21967828/}}
#* {{quote-av|en|author=Paul Simms|authorlink=Paul Simms|actor={{w|Matt Berry}}|role=Laszlo Cravensworth|episode={{w|The Return of Jerry}}|title={{w|What We Do in the Shadows}}|url=https://www.hulu.com/watch/3e89593c-1780-49cd-a186-6d62389e95f9|season=6|number=1|date=October 21, 2024|time=22:41|text=“Conquering the New World is indeed job number one. It is of the '''utmost''' importance. But is it as important as creating life?”}}

